<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-jiuquan ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D / unknown payload (Jiuquan LA-94, SLS-2 / 603) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 17.00 s, kick 1.050 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 621 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.7457-0.002823*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Long March 2D (configuration 2, two-stage) (sim/vehicles/lm2d.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-2D TIMELINE mode: configuration-2 stage data (World Launch Vehicles 2nd ed. 2007 via huijiwiki) + SAST TYPICAL flight sequence (huijiwiki); all event times hard constraints. Typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s.
T0 = LL2 NET 2026-11-11T11:40:00Z (Wed 11 Nov 3:40 am PST; window 11:32-12:05Z; NOTAM ZLHW A5728/26 window identical). Payload and orbit unknown. Event times = SAST TYPICAL LM-2D sequence (huijiwiki), not this flight&#x27;s. UNTUNED: no altitude/range knots published.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 192.23 deg; payload 621 kg.
Pad: 40.960482N 100.298059E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-11T11:40:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+705.1 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+737 s; rows after cutoff tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+737 s (SAST typical LM-2D sequence via huijiwiki: payload separation T+737.1 s (TYPICAL, not flight-specific)): alt 499.68 km, osculating 498.8 x 501.9 km, i 97.764 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: Typical-sequence residual-propellant venting at T+1152.1 s (deorbit of S2 after separation) is not modelled; it does not affect the payload orbit.</description>
